APPROVED_CORPUS = [{'evidence_id': 'product_guide:1', 'source_id': 'product_guide', 'section_id': 'workspace_api_keys', 'excerpt': "This excerpt is adapted from Dify's own product documentation for support agents and the support-ticket assistant's knowledge base. It covers four areas: workspace and API key setup, connecting a model provider, building a basic RAG pipeline (Knowledge Pipeline), and billing/plan limits on Dify Cloud.", 'source_revision': '867363a847665a1b4afe68a2eeca23417c228780057e940cd1afd8e93f535110'}, {'evidence_id': 'product_guide:2', 'source_id': 'product_guide', 'section_id': 'workspace_api_keys', 'excerpt': 'Every Dify Cloud account belongs to at least one **workspace**, a shared container for apps, knowledge bases, team members, and billing. The person who creates a workspace becomes its owner; owners and admins can invite additional members from **Settings → Members**, where new invitees are assigned a role (Owner, Admin, Editor, or Normal member). Each workspace plan caps how many members can be active at once (see Section 4); if a workspace is downgraded below its current member count, the members over the new cap lose workspace access immediately until seats are freed or the plan is upgraded again.', 'source_revision': '867363a847665a1b4afe68a2eeca23417c228780057e940cd1afd8e93f535110'}, {'evidence_id': 'product_guide:3', 'source_id': 'product_guide', 'section_id': 'workspace_api_keys', 'excerpt': 'Dify issues two different kinds of API keys, and they are **not interchangeable**:', 'source_revision': '867363a847665a1b4afe68a2eeca23417c228780057e940cd1afd8e93f535110'}, {'evidence_id': 'product_guide:4', 'source_id': 'product_guide', 'section_id': 'workspace_api_keys', 'excerpt': '- **App API keys** authenticate calls to a specific published app (Chatbot, Agent, Workflow, or Chatflow). They are created from that app\'s own **API Access** (sometimes shown as "Monitoring → API Key") panel inside the app builder, by clicking **Create new Secret Key**. The key is shown once, prefixed `app-`, and must be stored by the developer immediately since Dify does not redisplay it later. An app\'s API key only works for that one app — a key created for one chatbot will return an authentication error if used against a different app\'s endpoint, even inside the same workspace.\n- **Dataset (knowledge base) API keys** authenticate calls to the Knowledge/dataset API — creating datasets, uploading documents, or querying a knowledge base directly without going through a published app. These are created from the dataset\'s own detail page, under its **Service API** panel, and are scoped only to the knowledge base(s) they were created against. A dataset key will not authenticate a request to an app endpoint, and an app key will not authenticate a dataset-API request.', 'source_revision': '867363a847665a1b4afe68a2eeca23417c228780057e940cd1afd8e93f535110'}, {'evidence_id': 'product_guide:5', 'source_id': 'product_guide', 'section_id': 'workspace_api_keys', 'excerpt': 'A fresh key that returns a `401 Unauthorized` almost always means one of: the wrong key type was used for the endpoint being called (app key vs. dataset key), the key was pasted with surrounding whitespace, or the app/dataset the key belongs to has since been deleted or unpublished. Rotating a compromised key is done by creating a new secret key and deleting the old one from the same panel; there is no separate "rotate" action.', 'source_revision': '867363a847665a1b4afe68a2eeca23417c228780057e940cd1afd8e93f535110'}, {'evidence_id': 'product_guide:6', 'source_id': 'product_guide', 'section_id': 'model_providers', 'excerpt': "Dify apps need at least one language model to run. Workspaces start with access to a small set of **Dify-hosted models** (from OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, xAI, and Tongyi) paid for out of the workspace's message-credit balance (Section 4). To move beyond the included credits, or to use a provider not offered on Dify-hosted credits, a workspace connects its **own** model provider:", 'source_revision': '867363a847665a1b4afe68a2eeca23417c228780057e940cd1afd8e93f535110'}, {'evidence_id': 'product_guide:7', 'source_id': 'product_guide', 'section_id': 'model_providers', 'excerpt': '1. Go to **Settings → Model Provider**, or open the **Marketplace** and filter by "Models."\n2. Install the plugin for the desired provider (OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure OpenAI, and others are published officially; additional community providers are also listed).\n3. Enter the credentials the provider requires — typically an API key, and for Azure OpenAI, also the resource endpoint URL and deployment name.\n4. Save, then set that provider\'s model as the default (or per-app override) under the app\'s **Model** settings.', 'source_revision': '867363a847665a1b4afe68a2eeca23417c228780057e940cd1afd8e93f535110'}, {'evidence_id': 'product_guide:8', 'source_id': 'product_guide', 'section_id': 'model_providers', 'excerpt': "Once a workspace supplies its own key for a provider, calls to that provider's models are billed directly by the provider and no longer draw down the workspace's Dify message credits. Message credits and bring-your-own-key billing can be mixed per app: one app can run on Dify-hosted credits while another, in the same workspace, runs on a connected OpenAI key.", 'source_revision': '867363a847665a1b4afe68a2eeca23417c228780057e940cd1afd8e93f535110'}, {'evidence_id': 'product_guide:9', 'source_id': 'product_guide', 'section_id': 'model_providers', 'excerpt': "Message credits are not consumed at a flat rate. Each model response is metered in credits according to the specific model used — lighter models (for example smaller GPT variants) consume as little as 1 credit per response, mid-tier models around 5 credits, and larger or multimodal models (audio transcription, text-to-speech, flagship chat models) around 10 credits per response. A workspace that mostly uses a heavier model will exhaust its credit balance noticeably faster than the headline credit number suggests. Once a workspace's credits are used up, model calls on Dify-hosted credits stop working until the workspace either connects its own API key for that provider or waits for the next monthly credit reset (paid plans) — Sandbox credits do not reset.", 'source_revision': '867363a847665a1b4afe68a2eeca23417c228780057e940cd1afd8e93f535110'}, {'evidence_id': 'product_guide:10', 'source_id': 'product_guide', 'section_id': 'model_providers', 'excerpt': 'Model providers unrelated to standard chat/completion — for example self-hosted or local model runtimes — are managed the same way, through a provider plugin in the Marketplace, if a published plugin exists for that runtime; this guide does not enumerate which self-hosted runtimes currently have an official plugin.', 'source_revision': '867363a847665a1b4afe68a2eeca23417c228780057e940cd1afd8e93f535110'}, {'evidence_id': 'product_guide:11', 'source_id': 'product_guide', 'section_id': 'rag_pipeline', 'excerpt': "A Knowledge Pipeline turns uploaded files or connected data sources into a searchable **dataset** that an app's retrieval node can query. Every document a pipeline ingests passes through four stages, in order: **Parse → Enrich → Chunk → Embed/Index**.", 'source_revision': '867363a847665a1b4afe68a2eeca23417c228780057e940cd1afd8e93f535110'}, {'evidence_id': 'product_guide:12', 'source_id': 'product_guide', 'section_id': 'rag_pipeline', 'excerpt': "- **Parse** extracts raw text from the source file (PDF, DOCX, Markdown, website, Notion page, etc.).\n- **Enrich** applies optional cleanup steps, such as stripping boilerplate or extracting tables.\n- **Chunk** splits the parsed text into retrievable units, using one of three chunking modes chosen when the dataset is created or a document is added: **General** (fixed-size segments with configurable overlap), **Parent-Child** (a small child chunk is embedded and matched, but its larger parent chunk is returned to the model for fuller context), or **Q&A** (the pipeline generates question/answer pairs from the source text, useful for FAQ-style content).\n- **Embed/Index** converts each chunk into a retrievable record, using one of two indexing techniques: **Economical** (keyword-based index, free, does not count against the workspace's Knowledge Data Storage quota) or **High Quality** (vector embeddings via the workspace's embedding model, which does count against the plan's Knowledge Data Storage quota and stops accepting new documents once that quota is full).", 'source_revision': '867363a847665a1b4afe68a2eeca23417c228780057e940cd1afd8e93f535110'}, {'evidence_id': 'product_guide:13', 'source_id': 'product_guide', 'section_id': 'rag_pipeline', 'excerpt': 'When a document is edited and saved, it is re-processed through these same four stages before its chunks are available for retrieval again; a newly indexed document is not searchable mid-processing.', 'source_revision': '867363a847665a1b4afe68a2eeca23417c228780057e940cd1afd8e93f535110'}, {'evidence_id': 'product_guide:14', 'source_id': 'product_guide', 'section_id': 'rag_pipeline', 'excerpt': 'Before publishing an app that uses a dataset, the **Hit Testing** / retrieval-test panel on the dataset page lets a builder type a sample query and see exactly which chunks would be retrieved and their similarity scores, without needing to run the full app. Retrieval behavior in a live app is governed by settings on the retrieval node: **top_k** (how many chunks to return), an optional **score threshold** (chunks scoring below it are discarded even if they would otherwise be in the top_k), and whether **reranking** is enabled via a connected rerank model. A retrieval step that returns no results is most often explained by the score threshold being set too high, the document still being mid-indexing, or the query simply not matching any ingested content — not by an account or provider-propagation delay.', 'source_revision': '867363a847665a1b4afe68a2eeca23417c228780057e940cd1afd8e93f535110'}, {'evidence_id': 'product_guide:15', 'source_id': 'product_guide', 'section_id': 'rag_pipeline', 'excerpt': "Each workspace plan caps the number of knowledge documents and the Knowledge Data Storage a dataset can consume; see Section 4. A request that would push either over the plan's cap is rejected at upload time with an error naming the limit, rather than silently truncating the document set.", 'source_revision': '867363a847665a1b4afe68a2eeca23417c228780057e940cd1afd8e93f535110'}, {'evidence_id': 'product_guide:16', 'source_id': 'product_guide', 'section_id': 'billing_plans', 'excerpt': 'Dify Cloud is billed per **workspace**, not per individual seat, across four tiers. Monthly and annual billing are both offered; annual billing is discounted roughly 17% versus paying monthly.', 'source_revision': '867363a847665a1b4afe68a2eeca23417c228780057e940cd1afd8e93f535110'}, {'evidence_id': 'product_guide:17', 'source_id': 'product_guide', 'section_id': 'billing_plans', 'excerpt': '| Plan | Price | Message credits | Team members | Apps | Knowledge documents | Knowledge data storage | API rate limit |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Sandbox | Free | 200 credits, one-time (does not renew) | 1 | 5 | 50 | 50 MB | 5,000 calls/month |\n| Professional | $59/workspace/month ($590/year) | 5,000 credits/month | 3 | 50 | 500 | 5 GB | No Dify-imposed API rate limit |\n| Team | $159/workspace/month ($1,590/year) | 10,000 credits/month | 50 | 200 | 1,000 | 20 GB | No Dify-imposed API rate limit |\n| Enterprise | Custom (contact sales) | Custom | Custom | Custom | Custom | Custom | Custom |', 'source_revision': '867363a847665a1b4afe68a2eeca23417c228780057e940cd1afd8e93f535110'}, {'evidence_id': 'product_guide:18', 'source_id': 'product_guide', 'section_id': 'billing_plans', 'excerpt': "Only the workspace **owner** and **admins** can open the Billing page and manage a subscription. Payment is by credit card by default; paying by invoice or bank transfer is still being evaluated by Dify and, if it ships, is expected to be limited to annual Team subscriptions only — it is not available on any plan today. If a workspace's usage (documents, storage, or team members) exceeds the limits of a lower plan after a downgrade, the resources or members above the new plan's cap become inaccessible rather than being deleted; restoring access requires upgrading again or reducing usage back under the new plan's limits.", 'source_revision': '867363a847665a1b4afe68a2eeca23417c228780057e940cd1afd8e93f535110'}, {'evidence_id': 'product_guide:19', 'source_id': 'product_guide', 'section_id': 'billing_plans', 'excerpt': "Enterprise is a separately sold, typically self-hosted or VPC-deployed product line for organizations that need capabilities beyond what any Cloud tier offers, such as single sign-on, detailed audit logging, and a dedicated customer success manager; Enterprise pricing and feature scope are negotiated directly with Dify's sales team rather than published, and this guide does not detail Enterprise configuration.", 'source_revision': '867363a847665a1b4afe68a2eeca23417c228780057e940cd1afd8e93f535110'}, {'evidence_id': 'product_guide:20', 'source_id': 'product_guide', 'section_id': 'billing_plans', 'excerpt': 'This excerpt focuses on day-to-day workspace, model-provider, Knowledge Pipeline, and Cloud-billing questions. It does not document Enterprise-only configuration (SSO/SAML setup, audit-log export formats, compliance certifications), self-hosted/Community Edition deployment, the plugin SDK for building custom integrations, or workflow-level orchestration features beyond the retrieval node settings described above. Questions in those areas should be routed to the appropriate specialist team rather than answered from this material alone.', 'source_revision': '867363a847665a1b4afe68a2eeca23417c228780057e940cd1afd8e93f535110'}, {'evidence_id': 'api_transport_supplement:1', 'source_id': 'api_transport_supplement', 'section_id': 'http_authorization', 'excerpt': 'The official [Dify API guide](https://docs.dify.ai/en/api-reference/guides/get-started) documents sending the applicable API key as a Bearer token in the HTTP Authorization header. Make these calls from a backend so the key is not exposed in client code.', 'source_revision': '2d17e31b5d1129359b46a107284bab197e3002329ae19be9aeaec278dc247078'}, {'evidence_id': 'api_transport_supplement:2', 'source_id': 'api_transport_supplement', 'section_id': 'http_authorization', 'excerpt': "Use this source only for those transport claims. The user-supplied fictional product guide remains the authority for this demo's key-creation UI, key scope, model-provider policies and plan limits. This supplement does not make a Dify app key an OpenAI provider key or authorize replacing fixture policies with current Cloud policies.", 'source_revision': '2d17e31b5d1129359b46a107284bab197e3002329ae19be9aeaec278dc247078'}]


def main(chunks: list) -> dict:
    if not isinstance(chunks, list) or len(chunks) > 64:
        raise ValueError('Retrieval chunks must be an array of at most 64 records.')
    evidence = []
    seen = set()
    for chunk in chunks:
        if not isinstance(chunk, dict):
            continue
        content = chunk.get('content')
        metadata = chunk.get('metadata', {})
        if not isinstance(content, str) or not content.strip() or not isinstance(metadata, dict):
            continue
        title, name = chunk.get('title'), metadata.get('document_name')
        if title and name and title != name:
            continue
        source_id = DOCUMENT_SOURCES.get(name or title)
        if source_id is None:
            continue
        excerpt = content.strip()
        matches = [record for record in APPROVED_CORPUS
                   if record['source_id'] == source_id and excerpt in record['excerpt']]
        if len(matches) != 1:
            continue
        record = matches[0]
        evidence_id = record['evidence_id'] + ':' + hashlib.sha256(excerpt.encode()).hexdigest()[:16]
        if evidence_id in seen:
            continue
        seen.add(evidence_id)
        evidence.append(dict(record, evidence_id=evidence_id, excerpt=excerpt))
    return {'evidence': evidence, 'context': json.dumps(evidence, ensure_ascii=False)}
